      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "आभोग enjoyment in full ( आ ); or with Râmarshi, परिपूर्णता. Cf.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "०ग्रासैकबद्धस्पृह Nit. 29.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 97. तत्त्व &c.—whose intellect is keen in discerning",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "( thinking out ) the truth, discrimination of the real from the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "unreal. उत्तम &c.—wise men do not care what others speak",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "about them, but silently go their own way. स्वयं—स्वेनैव रूपेण",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "आनन्दवन्तः । ‘by themselves; Râmarshi or without meddling",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "with others’ will also do.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 98. मरुत् अशनं कल्पितं—In such constructions the noun",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "used to complete the sense of verbs of incomplete predication",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "is put in the Nom. case; See A. G. § 12. ( a ). हिंसाशून्यम्—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "free from the sin of causing the destruction of animal life Cf.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "Goldsmith—“And from the mountain’s grassy side. A guilt-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "less feast I bring.” पशवः—beasts are created so as to live on",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "grass. स्थलीशायिनः—lying on the lawn; स्थली means a natural",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "plot of land. संसार &c —To those that do not possess the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "faculty of reason, God has assigned a cheap, easy livelihood;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "but to those who can think out the means of their salvation",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "( i. e. men ) He has assigned a mode of life in pursuit of which",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "all their good qualities are exhausted. The struggle for",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "existence, in the case of man, engrosses all his energies, and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "leaves him neither time, nor energy to seek eternal bliss. It is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "difficult to see the bearing of this sl. here. Probably the poet",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "means—Men should, therefore, feel disgust for worldly life and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 17,
          "text": "direct their efforts to the acquistion of Moksha.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 99. पद्मासनं is a particular posture in religious me-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "ditation, thus described:—उत्तानौ चरणौ कृत्वा ऊरुसंस्थौ प्रय-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "त्नतः । ऊरुमध्ये तथोत्तानौ पाणी पद्मासनं त्विदम् ॥ Or ऊरुमूले &c. see",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "com: योगनिद्रा—A sleep of meditation or contemplation. योगी",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "मनसो विषयान्तरव्यावृत्तिः तद्रूपा निद्रा । contemplation of the mind",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "on Brahma is here likened to sleep because the Yogî is dead to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "the external world during the time of mediation–his mind takes",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "cognisance of no external objects like that of a man fast asleep.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "किं तैर्भाव्यम्—will they ever be ? कण्डूयन्ते-A denom. from कण्डू",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
